# Vercel builds two services from this repository, the frontend (web/) and the read
# API (api/), and nothing else. Everything below stays out of the upload: the
# collector and its configuration, the metrics pipeline, its tests and scripts,
# migrations, docs, CI workflows, fixtures and installs. Root files such as
# vercel.json and README.md are still uploaded. tests/test_deploy_config.py fails
# if a file a service is built from is removed.
/collector/
/config/
/docs/
/.github/
.venv
**/.venv
node_modules
**/node_modules
.fixtures
metrics
tests
scripts
# A bare name matches at any depth, so `scripts` also matches web/scripts/. Its
# check-bundle.mjs is a build gate that `npm run build` runs, so it stays in the upload
# (tests/test_deploy_config.py).
!web/scripts/
!web/scripts/**
supabase
api/tests
web/dist
